---
permalink: /admin/account/
title: "Account | Admin"
bodyScripts:
  - src: "/scripts/admin-account.js"
    type: "module"
  - src: "/scripts/contact-widget.js"
    type: "module"
  - src: "/scripts/palette.js"
    type: "module"
---
<section class="app-page">
  <div class="app-prose">

    {# Back to the list rather than a breadcrumb trail: there is exactly one place this page is
       reached from, and naming it is more use than drawing the hierarchy. #}
    <a href="/admin/accounts/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-brand-muted hover:text-brand-accent">
      {% icon "fa-solid-arrow-right", "h-3 w-3 rotate-180" %}<span>All accounts</span>
    </a>

    {# The heading is the person. It is filled in by the script once the account is loaded, and
       holds a non-breaking space until then so nothing below it moves when it arrives. #}
    <h1 id="who" class="mt-4 text-3xl font-bold text-brand-text">&nbsp;</h1>
    <p id="whoEmail" class="text-brand-muted"></p>
    <div id="whoMeta" class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2"></div>

    <div id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="mt-6 text-sm"></div>

    <div id="panels" class="hidden">

      <!-- Name -->
      <section aria-labelledby="name-heading" class="card mt-8">
        <h2 id="name-heading" class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-text">Name</h2>
        <p class="hint mt-1">
          Shown to them when they sign in, and to you in the accounts list. Clearing both leaves
          the account with no name, which is what it had before anyone typed one.
        </p>
        <form id="nameForm" method="post" novalidate class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div>
            <label for="accFirst" class="field-label">First name</label>
            <input type="text" id="accFirst" name="accFirst" autocomplete="off" maxlength="60" class="field">
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="accLast" class="field-label">Last name</label>
            <input type="text" id="accLast" name="accLast" autocomplete="off" maxlength="60" class="field">
          </div>
          <div class="sm:col-span-2">
            <button type="submit" class="btn-primary">Save name</button>
          </div>
        </form>
      </section>

      <!-- Password reset -->
      <section aria-labelledby="reset-heading" class="card mt-6">
        <h2 id="reset-heading" class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-text">Password</h2>
        <p class="hint mt-1">
          Emails them a link to choose a new one. Their current password keeps working until they
          use it, and the link works once.
        </p>

        {# The confirmation is a disclosure rather than a browser dialog: it names the address
           the mail will go to, which is the fact worth checking before pressing anything, and a
           confirm() cannot show it. Nothing is sent by opening it. #}
        <div class="mt-4">
          <button type="button" id="resetOpen" class="btn-secondary">Send a password reset…</button>
          <div id="resetConfirm" class="hidden mt-4 rounded-lg border border-brand-accent/30 bg-brand-accent/5 p-4">
            <p class="text-sm text-brand-text">
              Email a password reset link to <span id="resetTarget" class="font-semibold"></span>?
            </p>
            <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
              <button type="button" id="resetGo" class="btn-primary text-sm">Yes, send it</button>
              <button type="button" id="resetCancel" class="btn-secondary text-sm">Cancel</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Email address -->
      <section aria-labelledby="email-heading" class="card mt-6">
        <h2 id="email-heading" class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-text">Email address</h2>
        <p class="hint mt-1">
          This is how they sign in. Nothing changes when you press send: a confirmation goes to
          the new address and the move happens only when somebody opens it. Their current address
          keeps working until then, and is told that you asked.
        </p>

        <form id="emailForm" method="post" novalidate class="mt-4">
          <label for="accEmail" class="field-label">New email address</label>
          <input type="email" id="accEmail" name="accEmail" autocomplete="off" maxlength="254"
            aria-describedby="status" class="field">
          <button type="button" id="emailOpen" class="btn-secondary mt-4">Move this account…</button>

          <div id="emailConfirm" class="hidden mt-4 rounded-lg border border-amber-600/40 bg-amber-600/5 p-4">
            <p class="text-sm text-brand-text">
              Ask <span id="emailTarget" class="font-semibold"></span> to take over this account?
            </p>
            <p class="hint mt-2">
              If that address is wrong, whoever holds it can take the account by confirming. It
              is worth reading twice.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
              <button type="submit" class="btn-primary text-sm">Yes, send the confirmation</button>
              <button type="button" id="emailCancel" class="btn-secondary text-sm">Cancel</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </form>
      </section>

    </div>

  </div>
</section>
